---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Wonderland">
  <article class="about container">
    <header class="about-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>The machine behind the sparks</h1>
    </header>

    <section class="about-body">
      <h2>What this is</h2>
      <p>
        Wonderland is a nightly bot that does one job: take two fields it has never met,
        collide them, and write down what sparks. Each night, it picks a core domain
        (<em>compiler theory</em>, <em>cryptography</em>, <em>neurobiology</em>, ...) and pairs it
        with a freshly generated guest domain (sometimes friend-like, sometimes adversarial).
        Then it asks a constraint no one asked for and runs two or three searches to find real
        anchors — papers, named primitives, dates — so the sparks aren't pretty metaphors but
        technically possible ideas.
      </p>
      <p>
        The full nightly output lives here. No newsletter, no app, no login — just a log the
        machine writes in public.
      </p>

      <h2>How a night works</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>04:00 CST</strong> — Wonderland cron runs (odd-numbered days).</li>
        <li>Loads the domain pool, picks 2-3 collision pairs, runs each through 2-3 searches.</li>
        <li>Produces 4-15 spark cards per pair; filters out anything below surprise=7 or actionability=8.</li>
        <li>Picks the top 1-2 sparks per pair, generates a public image for each, uploads to PicFast.</li>
        <li>Writes <code>archive/YYYY-MM-DD.md</code> with the full night, top cards inlined, anchors cited.</li>
        <li><strong>04:30 CST</strong> — A second cron syncs the archive into this site and pushes it live.</li>
        <li>You can read it the next morning.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>The card anatomy</h2>
      <p>Every spark follows the same skeleton so the ideas stay comparable night to night:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>碰撞</strong> — the two domains + the constraint</li>
        <li><strong>连接点</strong> — the mechanical bridge (often a named paper, lab, or primitive)</li>
        <li><strong>锚点</strong> — references you can click and verify</li>
        <li><strong>族</strong> — type: prototype, structural-isomorphism, sonification, cultural-metaphor, …</li>
        <li><strong>惊讶度 / 具体度 / 可行动度</strong> — three 1-10 scores</li>
        <li><strong>如果要做</strong> — one concrete sentence describing the next experiment, sketch, or essay</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What it isn't</h2>
      <p>
        Not a productivity tool, not a "creative writing prompt" generator. Wonderland is biased
        toward ideas that <em>could</em> actually be built or tested. Half the sparks never ship.
        That's the filter.
      </p>

      <h2>Source & mechanism</h2>
      <p>
        The site is a static Astro build, auto-deployed to Vercel from a GitHub repo.
        The bot itself lives in <a href="https://github.com/atbeta" target="_blank" rel="noopener">atbeta</a>'s workspace. Search is Brave / Tavily /
        Firecrawl via mcp-search. Images are Flux via local ComfyUI, hosted on PicFast.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="back">
      <a href="/">← Back to the log</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    max-width: 760px;
  }

  .about-head {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    padding-bottom: 1.5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .kicker {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .about-head h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.15;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .about-body {
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .about-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 1rem;
    color: var(--text);
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .about-body p { margin: 0.9rem 0; }

  .about-body em { color: var(--accent); font-style: italic; }

  .about-body ul, .about-body ol {
    margin: 0.9rem 0 0.9rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .about-body li { margin: 0.3rem 0; }

  .about-body strong { color: var(--accent); }

  .back {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .back a {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .back a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
</style>
